On 2009-12-20, Aaron <abchiptop@gmail.com> wrote:
> Is it considered bad form to do a clean install to clear out some
> particularly nasty bones files? 

In general, yes; bones can provide game-breaking benefit as well as
game-breaking disadvantage, and if you take one, you should take the
other as well.

You can take heart in one thing though: bones aren't guaranteed to be
re-saved just because you die there, and aren't guaranteed to be loaded
just because you hit that level.  Also remember that you don't have to
try to pass a particular bones level the minute you encounter it; this
both increases your chances of survival _and_ means that if you die
off-level, that bones is guaranteed to be gone forever.

